From d86f1add37db7ab125caff7742c3fca70615aae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:37:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native Host interface, subscription hub, pause,
 merkle and avalanche

Add the Host interface the core reaches the node through (chain view,
block storage, mempool/relay, process hooks), and port the indexer's
node-independent helpers from chronik-indexer:

- subs.rs/subs_group.rs: tokio-broadcast-equivalent channels (per
  receiver ring buffers; overflow drops the oldest and reports Lagged
  once), block/tx message types, and pluggable groups (txid, script with
  scripthash keys, token id, LOKAD id) keyed by serialized members.
  Capacities are Rust's: blocks 16, txs 32, per-group 16. Wakers run
  after the hub lock is released.
- pause.rs: -chronikallowpause pause/resume with the Rust error texts.
- merkle.rs: block merkle root/branch with a cached tree; SHA256d comes
  from a hook so the core links no node crypto.
- avalanche.rs: finalized height tracking.

Tests: 54 cases (all 10 merkle.rs tests ported; the other modules have
no Rust tests, so ring-buffer overflow, group fan-out/unsubscribe,
pause and avalanche behaviour are covered by new cases).

Tier: eCash
